    "examples": [
      {
        "input": "This is a task from an agent benchmark. Can you return the `mapped_rxn` associated with the template that, when applied to the molecule `COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O`, reproduces the reaction: A Dies-Alder reaction is a [4+2] cycloaddition between a conjugated diene and a dienophile, resulting generally in the formation of a six-membered ring. The reaction is stereospecific, meaning that the stereochemistry of the reactants is preserved in the product. The reaction typically proceeds via a concerted mechanism, where the pi electrons of the diene and dienophile interact to form new sigma bonds. The reaction can be catalyzed by heat or Lewis acids, and the regioselectivity of the product can be influenced by substituents on the diene and dienophile. As a result of the reaction, a new carbon-carbon bond is formed, and the order changes from C=C to C-C, and from C=C to C-C as well. Note that the hints are describing the forward reaction, but you have to perform the retrosynthetic step.\n\nBelow are a few scenarios that may contain an agent's correct/incorrect thought-action pairs.\n\nWhich scenario corresponds to a correct/incorrect tought-action pair?",
        "target_scores": {
          "<thought>\nLet me try with the next criteria\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_formed\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"bonds_order_changed\": [\"6-6 (2.0 -> 1.0)\", \"6-6 (2.0 -> 1.0)\"],\n \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 1.0,
          "<thought>\nLet me analyze this task step by step:\n\n1. I have a molecule: COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\n2. The task describes a Diels-Alder reaction (forward), which is a [4+2] cycloaddition between a diene and dienophile forming a six-membered ring\n3. I need to find the retrosynthetic template that would break this molecule back into its precursors\n4. The hint mentions that in the forward reaction:\n   - C=C bonds change to C-C bonds\n   - A new C-C bond is formed\n   - This is a cycloaddition forming a six-membered ring\n\nFor the retrosynthetic step (reverse of Diels-Alder):\n- I need to break C-C bonds that were formed\n- Some C-C bonds should change back to C=C bonds\n- The six-membered ring should be opened\n\nLet me start by searching for templates that match these criteria. Since this is a retrosynthetic step, I'm looking for templates that would:\n- Break C-C bonds (that were formed in the forward reaction)\n- Change bond orders from C-C to C=C (reverse of what happens in forward reaction)\n\nLet me search the template catalog with appropriate criteria.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"bonds_order_changed\": [\"6-6 (1.0->2.0)\"],\n  \"limit\": 20\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nThe search returned some templates, but they don't seem to be specifically for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis. Let me think about the Diels-Alder reaction more carefully:\n\nIn a Diels-Alder reaction (forward):\n- A diene (with two C=C bonds) reacts with a dienophile (with one C=C bond)\n- Forms a six-membered ring\n- Two new C-C sigma bonds are formed\n- The double bonds in the diene become single bonds in the ring\n- The double bond in the dienophile becomes a single bond in the ring\n- One double bond remains in the six-membered ring\n\nFor the retrosynthetic step (breaking the Diels-Alder product):\n- Break two C-C bonds in the six-membered ring\n- Some C-C bonds change to C=C bonds\n- The ring opens to form a diene and dienophile\n\nLooking at the molecule: COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\n\nThis appears to have a bicyclic structure with a six-membered ring. Let me search more specifically for Diels-Alder retrosynthesis templates. I should look for templates that break two C-C bonds and form C=C bonds.\n\nLet me try a different search with more specific criteria for a retro Diels-Alder.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\", \"6-6\"],\n  \"limit\": 30\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0,
          "<thought>\nLet me think about what would be characteristic of a retro Diels-Alder reaction. Since the forward reaction forms C-C bonds, the retro reaction breaks C-C bonds. Let me search for templates that break C-C bonds.\n</thought>\n\n<action>search_template_catalog_by_criteria</action>\n<action_input>\n{\n  \"molecule_smiles\": \"COC([C@]12CC=CC[C@H]1C(C2)=O)=O\",\n  \"bonds_broken\": [\"6-6\"],\n  \"limit\": 50\n}\n</action_input>": 0.0
        }
      }
